@startuml autoridad_y_estados
' Qué responde este diagrama: "how did you manage state?"
' Fuente de verdad: claves/directorio.json — no hay reglas por estado en el código.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  BorderColor #546E7A
  FontColor #263238
}

title The defect, and the state machine that fixes it

legend top
  <b>The 58 rows came from a missing state.</b>
  The closing function wrote "human" by default and the schema had no state meaning
  "a machine closed this" — so the only path to closing ran through the human one.
  Authority is not written per state in code: it comes from <b>claves/directorio.json</b>,
  which says which key may authorise which state.
endlegend

state "open" as abierta #FFF8E1
state "informed" as informada #E8F5E9
state "closed" as cerrada #E8F5E9
state "dismissed" as descartada #FFEBEE
state "closed with judgement" as juicio #FFEBEE
state "debt forgiven" as perdonada #FFEBEE

[*] --> abierta : request arrives\n(typed or spoken)

abierta --> informada : **agente-comercial**\nscope: informed only
abierta --> cerrada : **agente-curador**\nonly with provable evidence,\nafter ceiling + fence + co-signer
abierta --> abierta : returned unsigned\n(nothing proved)

abierta --> descartada : **persona-operador** only
abierta --> juicio : **persona-operador** only
abierta --> perdonada : **persona-operador** only

note right of descartada
  <b>The three red states are the ones that cost a customer something.</b>
  No machine key can reach them:
  Cloud KMS returns 403 to the
  agent's service account, and the
  refusal is Google's, not ours.
end note

note bottom
  <b>agente-curador</b> (MACHINE) → closed, open
  <b>agente-comercial</b> (MACHINE) → informed
  <b>persona-operador</b> (HUMAN) → closed, open, dismissed, closed-with-judgement, forgiven
  Verbatim from claves/directorio.json. Whoever controls that file controls who counts
  as human — which is why it lives in the repository, where a change leaves a commit.
end note

@enduml
